      "topic": {
        "text": "Implicit casting cannot convert a long value to an int because the long occupies 8 bytes while the int occupies 4 bytes.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "When a method returns a long but the variable is declared as an int, implicit casting fails; explicit casting must be used if the programmer knows the value fits into the smaller type.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    },
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "Casting a double result of Math.random() directly to int yields zero.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "Math.random() returns a value between 0 (inclusive) and 1 (exclusive); casting that double to int truncates the fractional part, producing 0.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    },
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "To obtain an integer between 0 and 100 from Math.random(), the entire expression must be multiplied before casting.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "Wrap the expression (Math.random() * 100) in parentheses and then cast the result to int; otherwise only the fractional part is cast, resulting in zero.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    },
